  "homeAboutDhuhrRakat": "4 Sunnah + 4 Fard + 2 Sunnah",
  "homeAboutDhuhrVirtue": "Part of the 12 voluntary rak'ahs a day for which Allah builds a house in Paradise.",
  "homeAboutDhuhrReference": "\"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs during a day and a night will have a house built for him in Paradise.\" (Sahih Muslim)",
  "homeAboutAsrTiming": "Begins when an object's shadow equals its length and lasts until sunset.",
  "homeAboutAsrRakat": "4 Fard",
  "homeAboutAsrVirtue": "Guarding this prayer is singled out for special reward and warning.",
  "homeAboutAsrReference": "\"Whoever misses the Asr prayer, it is as if he lost his family and his wealth.\" (Sahih al-Bukhari)",
  "homeAboutMaghribTiming": "Begins right after sunset and lasts until the red twilight disappears.",
  "homeAboutMaghribRakat": "3 Fard + 2 Sunnah",
  "homeAboutMaghribVirtue": "A time when supplications are especially encouraged.",
  "homeAboutMaghribReference": "\"There are two occasions when a fasting person rejoices... when he breaks his fast.\" (Sahih al-Bukhari, on the Maghrib fast-breaking)",
  "homeAboutIshaTiming": "Begins once the twilight fully disappears and lasts until midnight (or Fajr, per some views).",
  "homeAboutIshaRakat": "4 Fard + 2 Sunnah + Witr",
  "homeAboutIshaVirtue": "Praying Isha in congregation is equivalent to standing half the night in prayer.",
  "homeAboutIshaReference": "\"Whoever prays Isha in congregation, it is as if he prayed half the night.\" (Sahih Muslim)",
